  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce the complete Maven package. Author sources are removed before offline installation; Java and Kotlin callers replay after moving the installed tree and execute again after deleting all consumer sources, giving six executions per selection. Compiler probes check the generated API, Java and Kotlin Unit classes, Kotlin function references and result nullability. The full API checks direct and repeated parameters, Array, List, Option, Product, both Except branches, Holder.packet and the active Choice.packet.value field, including exact per-site constructors, normalization, complete rejected-input snapshots and recovery. Independent controls reject every missing or changed retained record and coordinated resource, model, package, probe and execution mutations. Checked-record JVM acceptance covers the established top-level Interval, Sized 3 and Bounded 0 101 forms plus the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copied positions. Generic, recursive and inherited records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Both author routes and full/result-only APIs reproduce complete Maven packages from two author roots, remove author sources, install offline, replay after relocation and execute again after deleting all consumer sources. The runs use JDK 22.0.2, Kotlin 2.2.0 and Lean 4.32.2 on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor and 64-bit machine words. Original receipts, retained package members, compiler probes, execution records and selected sources are archived; native libraries and the closed JAR retain exact identities without copied bytes. Constructor entry counts and peak memory are unmeasured. Hosted glibc 2.38 release-floor acceptance remains assigned to the recurring workflow.",
